{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:sec:LIMITATIONS_COVERAGE_GAPS", "content_sha256": "17498c987b12e5a2ca6269fa0a66b0ae049c6a78ad1f66d163e58c84e93e7907", "heading": "Limitations / Coverage Gaps", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Limitations / Coverage Gaps\n\nThe penalty catalogue covers the pack's excerpted reports (2023-11, 2024-06, 2024-11, 2025-06); other held sessions sit in sibling packs. One quotation window is truncated by the excerpt\ncap (the notation warning's continuation is outside the window and is not\nparaphrased). Sessions without public ERs remain source gaps of record. No canonical\nplanes were written."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:sec:RESEARCH_STATUS", "content_sha256": "25f39f6ef9c7167a8fd3f1c2bfb62aaffa907afb365eacde05f9c616b3289a9e", "heading": "Research Status", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Research Status\n\nGENERATED under SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005 (BL-008 pass 5) from the run's evidence\npack alone; validator of record tools/sib @ 357ace0a; claim QA r3 bound all citations\nto pack excerpts. Deepened under SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017 (D3 tranche 1): +3 records (EXM-043..045), zero-append (cited spans already held in the pack of record); claim QA re-bound all citations. Research artifact — evidence-backed, not canonical educational truth."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:rec:EXM-016", "content_sha256": "61fd23e78bbdaa77c0216aca643c11ae46cf6f7b0ce17c98f9043ccd7daa408c", "heading": "EXM-016", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-016", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-016", "text": "### EXM-016 — Failed printed instructions\n\n**Claim:** not following an explicit instruction voids the intended marks.\n**Evidence:** \"A few candidates failed to follow the instruction to draw another four\nparticles.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2023-11/4CH1-1C/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:rec:EXM-017", "content_sha256": "d8980c40b332e65bc8951e83a8fea9f07fb2679e7a880e2bd0fa967789148b6e", "heading": "EXM-017", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-017", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-017", "text": "### EXM-017 — Inattentive formula work and unclear subscripts\n\n**Claim:** organic-formula answers are penalised for ignoring the starting hydrocarbon\nand for unreadable subscripts.\n**Evidence:** \"Many correctly gave the formulae of two alkenes but some did not pay\nattention to the starting hydrocarbon formula and gave molecules that were too large\nor did not follow the formula for an alkene. Candidates need to take care to write\ntheir subscript numbers clearly wh...\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2023-11/4CH1-1C/er.pdf p4).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:rec:EXM-018", "content_sha256": "bf7bea3c4f40e825ffaec27f93342fcbd198b2053230fd987efa730ab6481287", "heading": "EXM-018", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-018", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-018", "text": "### EXM-018 — Method-reading failures\n\n**Claim:** not reading (or not understanding) the method's variable-control design\ncosts whole questions.\n**Evidence:** \"Question (a) was very poorly answered with the majority gaining no\nmarks. It appears that the candidates either did not read the method or did not\nunderstand the idea of keeping the variables constant.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2023-11/4CH1-2C/er.pdf p4).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:rec:EXM-019", "content_sha256": "c6e0bb830a631b5d7174e4cae4e1b24172f097c65889823feeb5962f694397a4", "heading": "EXM-019", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-019", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-019", "text": "### EXM-019 — Unlinked statements in multi-mark explanations\n\n**Claim:** the reports tie lost explanation marks directly to missing links between\nstatements.\n**Evidence:** \"There were four questions with 4, 5 or 6 marks. All of these were\nexplanations. Many of the candidates struggled with these questions and only the very\nbest scored full marks. They needed to link the statements to gain all the marks\"\n(SRC-ER-4CH1, 2024-06/4CH1-1CR/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:rec:EXM-020", "content_sha256": "5f2558ddf08cbe0eb6975d81767ec48d914b938dcd869ef6f3d236f65dbe43df", "heading": "EXM-020", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-020", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-020", "text": "### EXM-020 — Quantity confusions: mass number vs atomic number\n\n**Claim:** reaching for the wrong nuclear quantity is a named, recurring error.\n**Evidence:** \"A large majority of candidates gave sulfur as the answer. Oxygen was\nseen occasionally as they were using the mass number rather than the atomic number.\"\n(SRC-ER-4CH1, 2024-06/4CH1-2C/er.pdf p4).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:rec:EXM-021", "content_sha256": "2454c87d01eb0f4ac18609fc65b79632108b5c8f242e2a2cd9366720b56b5cb6", "heading": "EXM-021", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-021", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-021", "text": "### EXM-021 — Notation misuse\n\n**Claim:** misused notation loses marks even when the chemistry is broadly right.\n**Evidence:** \"However, a significant number of candidates lost a mark as they often\nreferred to an incorrect use of\" — the 2C November introduction's notation warning\n(SRC-ER-4CH1, 2023-11/4CH1-2C/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:rec:EXM-043", "content_sha256": "d8074972a8f0158ae46b125fd860ccfe464846ba87406ad8b0f2743eb28aa001", "heading": "EXM-043", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-043", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-043", "text": "### EXM-043 — Terminology confusion penalised in long responses\n\n**Claim:** the penalised long-response failures of 2025-06 are terminology failures, with the ene/ane confusion in Q09(c) named as the written-clarity instance. The penalty reading is precise: the marks were not lost to chemistry ignorance but to word-level precision — one letter's worth, ene versus ane — inside an otherwise reachable response. The general vagueness penalty other sessions state is here given a concrete, teachable instance.\n**Evidence:** \"Long-response questions proved challenging for those candidates who lacked a firm grasp of key terminology\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2025-06/4CH1-1C/er.pdf p3); the named instance: \"confusion between ene and ane in Q09(c)\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2025-06/4CH1-1C/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:rec:EXM-044", "content_sha256": "0424a9901787aa5018521325f2ce515c135df4c20d1fe940acfbab6c4d86a987", "heading": "EXM-044", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-044", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-044", "text": "### EXM-044 — Particle-label switches and subatomic spelling\n\n**Claim:** on the 2025-06 1C opening atom question even successful candidates leaked marks — label switches still scored, spelling did not. The part still paid 2 of 3 under the switch — a partial-credit signal — but the spelling note came with no such cushion. The teachable point is that atom-model openings are only free marks when labels and spellings are exact.\n**Evidence:** \"Where errors occurred, these were typically due to the proton and neutron labels being switched, which still resulted in 2 out of 3 marks being awarded.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2025-06/4CH1-1C/er.pdf p4); \"It is worth noting that the spelling of the subatomic particles was often poor.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2025-06/4CH1-1C/er.pdf p4).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "chunk_id": "EXM-04:rec:EXM-045", "content_sha256": "47f6e56a15892a0e5829fa1013a29da3270f328b90cdb3c0c16c390687555db7", "heading": "EXM-045", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "EXM-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-017", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-ER-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "6162cc770e8391e4a76d68919b88fd9f23081ce9"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "EXM-045", "research_family": "examiner_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": true, "mark_schemes": false, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "EXM-045", "text": "### EXM-045 — The reversible-reaction calculation few finished\n\n**Claim:** the 2025-06 2C reversible-reaction calculation in Q06(c) was a four-mark part that very few candidates completed. A four-mark reversible-reaction calculation late in the paper is a deliberate discriminator: the report's per-question verdicts place Q06(c) alongside the session's unusual Q02(e) as the difficulty spines of 2C.\n**Evidence:** \"Question 6 was about reversible reactions and a tricky calculation in Q06(c) with few candidates achieving four marks.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2025-06/4CH1-2C/er.pdf p3).\n; \"Question 2 was unusual and discriminated well.\" (SRC-ER-4CH1, 2025-06/4CH1-2C/er.pdf p3).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
